{"kind":"artifact","text":"The ui tree as main carries it at merge commit 8924b4d09fde8ebb2705deb127334d56baa94f3e, which landed the wire-type parity work approved by codex in ae256854 and ratified in 1a881c1a. (Records are named here by the trailing eight hex of their event id, as the previous artifact at this path did.)\n\nThe merge changed ui/src/lib/api.ts and ui/src/lib/work.ts, and added internal/wireparity/parity_test.go, which is recorded separately at its own path. api.ts now declares the four succession-health fields the server actually sends on an artifact — describes_superseded_world, unable_to_flare, succession_unrecorded and live_predecessors — and describes_superseded_world on a statement, so the browser can see the conditions that cause the most trouble in this log. The optional disputed field that no Go struct emits is gone from Commitment, and with it the dead branch on it in work.ts; the disputed status is still handled through ATTENTION_WORK_STATUSES, so nothing changes for a reader. From this commit the mirror is checked by a Go test, so drift between the browser's copy of the wire types and the Go types fails the suite instead of turning into undefined at run time.\n\nGates run at this exact commit in the main checkout: go vet ./..., go build ./..., go test ./internal/... -count=1 (every package ok, including internal/docset and the new internal/wireparity) and npx tsc --noEmit in ui/. All passed.\n\nSuccession. This retires six live predecessors at this path: f2b297c3, 5e33e902, 8d78da85, 070e4f89, 610502ce and b8a53823. It also retires 2605d6f0 at ui/src/lib/api.ts with a bare supersession, because the wider path wins and this record is where the area continues.\n\n9dc0be22 at this path stays live, and still deliberately. Five pages cite it — docs/concepts/components.md, docs/reference/architecture.md, docs/reference/gs/serve.md, docs/reference/limits.md and docs/reference/mcp/presence.md — so retiring it would leave all five pointing at a withdrawn record and take the docset gate red; the guard added in ff6132ec refuses exactly that, and it is right to. I checked by grepping the tracked tree for each of the nine live artifact ids covering this merge; 9dc0be22 is the only one any file cites. Re-anchoring those five pages onto this record and then retiring 9dc0be22 is ordinary implementing work and needs its own request. Until then this path carries two live artifacts, and a reader should treat this one as what main carries.\n\nIt rests on ca8b65c9 at cmd/gs (event sha 7d105ca8f6b47fd6e6d526a8dc0a1477ca8b65c9), live and not stale, rather than on any record this merge retires or on the review of the merged head, so the retirements recorded next do not make it stale from birth.","body":{"commit":"8924b4d09fde8ebb2705deb127334d56baa94f3e","path":"ui"}}